# Rubix Lab host list - copy to hosts.txt and fill in your real addresses.
#
# One host per line:   <ip or hostname>  [role]
# Blank lines and anything after # are ignored.
#
# hosts.txt only records two kinds of FIXED, DURABLE facts about a host:
#
#   1. Infrastructure role - a permanent identity for that machine:
#        fullnode     - the dedicated fullnode for this environment
#        explorer     - the dedicated explorer for this environment
#        controller   - this machine (list it if it also runs a node)
#      Leave the role column blank for every other host.
#
#      One more tag exists, and it is NOT an infrastructure role:
#        multidid   - this machine deliberately carries a SECOND DID.
#      Every other host is held to exactly one DID and is excluded from a run
#      if it has more, because CreateDID is not idempotent and a surprise
#      second identity normally means something went wrong. A multidid host
#      opts out of that guard. It still takes part in tests as an ordinary
#      pool member; it simply also carries a spare DID for the cases that need
#      two on one machine - a same-node transfer cannot be built any other way.
#      One or two such hosts is enough; do not tag the whole fleet.
#
#   2. Unavailable - comment the line out with a reason + date, so every
#      tool (check-nodes.py, setup-ssh.sh, dids-to-excel.py, node-versions.py)
#      skips it automatically, without losing the record of why:
#        # 10.0.0.20  # down - unreachable since 2026-08-18
#
# Do NOT write "quorum" or "participant" here. Those are per-test-case
# assignments made at test-execution time from whatever hosts are left
# after excluding fixed-role and down hosts - not a fixed property of a
# host, since which machines act as quorum can change between test cycles.

10.0.0.11  fullnode
10.0.0.12  explorer
10.0.0.13  controller
10.0.0.20
10.0.0.21  multidid
10.0.0.22
